# Notice

This repository is a hand-maintained Python project template with an in-repo
`bootstrap` command. It is not a Cookiecutter (or similar scaffolding) template.

## Project license chosen at bootstrap

The template itself ships under MIT (`LICENSE`). When you run bootstrap, you may
keep MIT or select another supported SPDX id. Bootstrap writes a project
`LICENSE` file for the chosen id.

For some choices, bootstrap writes the full conventional license text (for
example MIT and BSD-3-Clause). For Apache-2.0 and MPL-2.0, bootstrap writes the
short copyright / notice form commonly used with those licenses, not the full
license body. Use the official texts as the authoritative license terms:

- Apache License 2.0:
  https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0
  (also linked from the short form as http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0)
- Mozilla Public License 2.0:
  https://www.mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/
  (also linked from the short form as https://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/)

If your distribution policy requires a full copy of Apache-2.0 or MPL-2.0 in
the repository, replace or supplement the generated `LICENSE` with the official
full text from the URLs above (or distribute that full text alongside the short
notice).
